      "writtenOn": "2022-02-07T23:01:06Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Good question. In theory it should, as I believe \u003cmethods\u003e is a strict superset of \u003cinit\u003e. That said, it\u0027s not clear to me why it\u0027s common to see separate rules that keep \u003cfields\u003e and \u003cmethods\u003e, rather than just using *.\n\n@Rico or @Christoffer do you know? Here are some examples:\n\nhttps://source.corp.google.com/piper///depot/google3/gmscore/sdk/config/proguard/base.pgcfg;rcl\u003d416077209;l\u003d113\n\nhttps://source.corp.google.com/piper///depot/google3/gmscore/sdk/config/proguard/base.pgcfg;rcl\u003d416077209;l\u003d299\n\nI\u0027m also wondering if we should include `includedescriptorclasses` on this rule as well. Thoughts?",
